{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25890164",
      "title": "What & Why?",
      "sourceHash": "881d46c4f6e23da6d99bff03ff3afe97350eaa647c10f63dbd841cee19bb359d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.12,
          "end": 4.16,
          "en": "So what is TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.16,
          "end": 6.77,
          "en": "and why would you use it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.77,
          "end": 11.77,
          "en": "TypeScript is a so-called \"superset\" to JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.8,
          "end": 16.65,
          "en": "It's a programming language which builds up on JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.65,
          "end": 19.644,
          "en": "It extends JavaScript you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.644,
          "end": 22.05,
          "en": "and that is really important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.05,
          "end": 26.424,
          "en": "The core programming language still, is JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.424,
          "end": 30.06,
          "en": "So the base JavaScript syntax you know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.06,
          "end": 32.53,
          "en": "how you write JavaScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.53,
          "end": 37.53,
          "en": "if statements, for loops, objects, all that does not change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 37.77,
          "end": 41.56,
          "en": "But TypeScript then adds more features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.56,
          "end": 46.18,
          "en": "to the JavaScript syntax, and that's also important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.18,
          "end": 51,
          "en": "Unlike React, TypeScript is not a library for JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 51,
          "end": 53.89,
          "en": "so it doesn't use JavaScript features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 53.89,
          "end": 57.36,
          "en": "to build new features on top of them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 57.36,
          "end": 60.11,
          "en": "to build functionalities around them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 60.11,
          "end": 64.35,
          "en": "But instead it extends the core JavaScript syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 64.35,
          "end": 69.35,
          "en": "and most importantly, it adds static typing to JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 70.62,
          "end": 74.22,
          "en": "And that's also where the name comes from, TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 74.22,
          "end": 77.615,
          "en": "It adds static typing to JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 77.615,
          "end": 82.615,
          "en": "because JavaScript on its own is actually dynamically typed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 83.28,
          "end": 86.88,
          "en": "And what does this mean and why is this useful?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 86.88,
          "end": 90.44,
          "en": "For this, I prepared a very simple example here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 90.44,
          "end": 92.25,
          "en": "which you find attached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 92.25,
          "end": 94.47,
          "en": "This is not a React app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 94.47,
          "end": 98.03999999999999,
          "en": "this is a standard JavaScript function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 98.03999999999999,
          "end": 103,
          "en": "and a standard HTML file, which has no actual content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 103,
          "end": 106.083,
          "en": "but which imports this script file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 107.19,
          "end": 109.74000000000001,
          "en": "Now, if I open this file in the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 109.74000000000001,
          "end": 112.41,
          "en": "simply by copying the path here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 112.41,
          "end": 115.69,
          "en": "and then opening that path in the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 115.69,
          "end": 118.78,
          "en": "if I reload this page and open the developer tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 118.78,
          "end": 121.94,
          "en": "I see seven here in the developer tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 121.94,
          "end": 124.2,
          "en": "in the JavaScript console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 124.2,
          "end": 127.935,
          "en": "And I see seven here because in this script file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 127.935,
          "end": 130.13,
          "en": "I define an \"add\" function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 130.13,
          "end": 132.17,
          "en": "and then I call this \"add\" function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 132.17,
          "end": 134.51,
          "en": "and store the result in this constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 134.51,
          "end": 138.17000000000002,
          "en": "and then I log this constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 138.17000000000002,
          "end": 142.672,
          "en": "So that's standard JavaScript, nothing fancy here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 142.672,
          "end": 146.04,
          "en": "Now JavaScript has types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 146.04,
          "end": 149.36,
          "en": "JavaScript knows the concept of types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 149.36,
          "end": 152.54,
          "en": "For example, here, the two values which I'm passing in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 152.54,
          "end": 154.95,
          "en": "are of type \"number\",",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 154.95,
          "end": 157.47,
          "en": "and that's something JavaScript knows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 157.47,
          "end": 160.37,
          "en": "on its own, without TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 160.37,
          "end": 162.66,
          "en": "The important thing just is that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 162.66,
          "end": 167.16,
          "en": "JavaScript as I just mentioned, is dynamically typed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 167.16,
          "end": 169.82999999999998,
          "en": "Which means that this function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 169.82999999999998,
          "end": 173.18,
          "en": "does not expect any particular types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 173.18,
          "end": 176.41,
          "en": "It just knows that it will receive two parameters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 176.41,
          "end": 177.87,
          "en": "and that's it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.87,
          "end": 179.79,
          "en": "So it's not statically typed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 179.79,
          "end": 184.4,
          "en": "the types for this function are not announced ahead of time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 184.4,
          "end": 186.82,
          "en": "instead it just takes whatever it gets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 186.82,
          "end": 189.73,
          "en": "and then tries to execute this code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 189.73,
          "end": 193.4,
          "en": "And that code happens to work with numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 193.4,
          "end": 198.17000000000002,
          "en": "But this code also happens to work with strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 198.17000000000002,
          "end": 202.2,
          "en": "And hence, if I convert my two numbers into strings here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 202.2,
          "end": 204.47,
          "en": "by wrapping them with quotes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 204.47,
          "end": 207.3,
          "en": "then I got two different types here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 207.3,
          "end": 209.93,
          "en": "I got two strings instead of numbers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 209.93,
          "end": 212.43,
          "en": "which are types JavaScript knows.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 212.43,
          "end": 215.07,
          "en": "And if I change it like this and saved as file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 215.07,
          "end": 219.31,
          "en": "if I reload, you see now we get 25 here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 219.31,
          "end": 221.71,
          "en": "because now the plus operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 221.71,
          "end": 226.19,
          "en": "does not add these two arguments in a mathematical way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 226.19,
          "end": 229,
          "en": "but instead it concatenates two strings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 229,
          "end": 232.2,
          "en": "because it receives two strings here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 232.2,
          "end": 237.2,
          "en": "And that shows why just JavaScript is okay and great,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 237.31,
          "end": 240.96,
          "en": "but why it might not always be best.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 240.96,
          "end": 245.93,
          "en": "Why having static typing could enhance your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 245.93,
          "end": 249.06,
          "en": "and prevent errors like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 249.06,
          "end": 251.6,
          "en": "Now, of course you might say, \"Which error?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 251.6,
          "end": 254.25,
          "en": "I can simply not call \"add\" like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 254.25,
          "end": 257.57,
          "en": "I just make sure that I always pass into numbers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 257.57,
          "end": 259.65,
          "en": "and it won't face this problem.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 259.65,
          "end": 262.48,
          "en": "And that's true, but in a bigger project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 262.48,
          "end": 264.26,
          "en": "with lots of code files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 264.26,
          "end": 267.74,
          "en": "and potentially a lot of people working on the code base,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 267.74,
          "end": 270.27,
          "en": "you might sometimes call a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 270.27,
          "end": 274.77,
          "en": "or use some object in an unintended way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 274.77,
          "end": 277.54,
          "en": "And then you could run into problems like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 277.54,
          "end": 279.77,
          "en": "because nothing is warning you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 279.77,
          "end": 283.14,
          "en": "that this is not how you should use this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 283.14,
          "end": 284.98,
          "en": "Nothing is telling you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 284.98,
          "end": 288.99,
          "en": "that this function actually wants two numbers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 288.99,
          "end": 292.82,
          "en": "instead of two strings or any values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 292.82,
          "end": 296.63,
          "en": "And that's where TypeScript can help us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 296.63,
          "end": 300.8,
          "en": "Because with TypeScript, and I'll show you this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 300.8,
          "end": 303.51,
          "en": "even though we haven't installed TypeScript yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 303.51,
          "end": 305.98,
          "en": "but I have it installed on my system already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 305.98,
          "end": 309.63,
          "en": "and we will install it together in the next lecture too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 309.63,
          "end": 311.56,
          "en": "But let me show you this first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 311.56,
          "end": 314.51,
          "en": "So with TypeScript, if I copy this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 314.51,
          "end": 317.61,
          "en": "what we will be able to do is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 317.61,
          "end": 320.76,
          "en": "we can add type annotations here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 320.76,
          "end": 323.94,
          "en": "simply by adding a colon after our parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 323.94,
          "end": 325.83,
          "en": "and then adding the type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 325.83,
          "end": 328.26,
          "en": "which should be used for this parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 328.26,
          "end": 330.51,
          "en": "I'll do this for B as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 330.51,
          "end": 334.33,
          "en": "And we'll also not just be able to use type annotations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 334.33,
          "end": 336.15,
          "en": "on function parameters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 336.15,
          "end": 338.82,
          "en": "but as you will see throughout this module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 338.82,
          "end": 342.053,
          "en": "we can use types and many other situations as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 342.98,
          "end": 344.71,
          "en": "So now I am making it clear,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 344.71,
          "end": 349.71,
          "en": "with TypeScript that here, I actually want two parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 350.35,
          "end": 352.9,
          "en": "which both should be of type number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 352.9,
          "end": 356.48,
          "en": "And hence, I already get an error here in my IDE,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 356.48,
          "end": 359.04,
          "en": "which tells me that this argument of type string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 359.04,
          "end": 361.963,
          "en": "is not assignable to a parameter of type number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 362.9,
          "end": 364.22,
          "en": "pretty helpful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 364.22,
          "end": 368.11,
          "en": "And with that, I can catch such an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 368.11,
          "end": 371.8,
          "en": "such an unintended use of this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 371.8,
          "end": 375.06,
          "en": "before I run and test my code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 375.06,
          "end": 376.48,
          "en": "And that of course allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 376.48,
          "end": 378.61,
          "en": "to write better code in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 378.61,
          "end": 380.65,
          "en": "because we can avoid such errors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 380.65,
          "end": 383.3,
          "en": "and we don't have to track them at runtime",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 383.3,
          "end": 387.8,
          "en": "but we see such errors right, when we start writing code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 387.8,
          "end": 391.953,
          "en": "And that's why using TypeScript could be worth a thought.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}